# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.
#
# Only the pipeline reads this. `pnpm run dev` needs nothing here — the Next.js
# app renders from the committed run.json and never calls the model, so the demo
# survives a missing key, a rate limit, or no network at all.

# Required by `pnpm run tracer` (and the full sweep in #4).
# Read by @ai-sdk/google under exactly this name — GEMINI_API_KEY is the CLI's
# variable and the SDK will not find it.
# Create one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# Before the first run, check two things in the AI Studio dashboard:
#
#   1. Tier. The free tier's terms say prompts and responses may be used to
#      improve Google products; the paid tier's say they are not. That interacts
#      with the hackathon's external-services rule — confirm with an organizer
#      before sending even synthetic data (PRD #1, still-open assumption).
#   2. Rate limit. It is not published in the docs, dashboard only, and it is
#      what `concurrency` in config/teams.json should be set from rather than
#      guessed (PRD #1 §Rabbit Holes — Effect.forEach defaults to 1).
